Since $1\text{ meter}=100\text{ centimeters}$, we know that both $\dfrac{1\text{ meter}}{100\text{ centimeters}}$ and $\dfrac{100\text{ centimeters}}{1\text{ meter}}$ equal $1$.

So we can multiply by either of those fractions to help us convert units, since multiplying by $1$ doesn't change value. In this problem, we multiply by $\blueD{\dfrac{100\text{ centimeters}}{1\text{ meter}}}$ since the quantity we want to convert is in $\text{meters}$:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}2\,\cancel{\text{meters}}\cdot \blueD{\dfrac{100 \text{ centimeters}}{1\,\,\cancel{\text{meter}}}}
\\\\
&=200\,\text{centimeters}
\end{align}$
